# Tests — local only, by request. They stay in the working tree and still run
# with `python -m pytest tests/`; they are simply not published.
#
# CONSEQUENCE, recorded so it is not rediscovered: CI can no longer run them.
# The pipeline is reduced to importing every app module, which still catches
# syntax errors, broken imports and circular dependencies across the codebase —
# but NOTHING else is verified on GitHub. All 1039 tests, and every
# database-layer control, are now verified only on this machine and on Railway
# via `python -m scripts.verify_invariants`.
/tests/

# Benchmark corpora built from REAL data. benchmarks/corpus.json.gz is
# synthetic and committed so CI can run the Phase-4 gate; anything named
# corpus-real* stores verbatim customer text and entity uuids and must never
# reach a public repository. scripts/make_benchmark refuses to write real data
# to any other name.
/benchmarks/corpus-real*.json.gz

# Claude Code workspace (skills, local settings) — local only.
.claude/

